1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:00,819
Hey!

2
00:00:00,819 --> 00:00:04,280
Let's make your first few minutes with IZ a little easier.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:10,087
If you've ever opened a treatment plan and thought, wait, which version is this, and what's missing?

4
00:00:10,087 --> 00:00:12,007
This is where IZ can help.

5
00:00:12,007 --> 00:00:17,651
It brings saved records, timing flags, and review evidence together on your Windows laptop.

6
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:20,517
Think of it as a helpful second set of eyes.

7
00:00:20,517 --> 00:00:22,184
You still bring the judgment.

8
00:00:22,184 --> 00:00:23,636
Let's walk through it.

9
00:00:24,416 --> 00:00:27,989
Start with the IZ desktop or Start Menu shortcut.

10
00:00:27,989 --> 00:00:31,259
Double click, then sign in with your assigned account.

11
00:00:31,259 --> 00:00:35,073
If you're asked to change a temporary password, do that first.

12
00:00:35,073 --> 00:00:37,585
Now open Status Dashboard.

13
00:00:37,585 --> 00:00:43,583
That's your starting point: what's saved, what needs attention, and whether the source is ready.

14
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:46,158
No need to learn every screen today.

15
00:00:46,158 --> 00:00:47,926
We'll start with one plan.

16
00:00:48,683 --> 00:00:50,312
Go to Patient Roster.

17
00:00:50,312 --> 00:00:55,968
Search by the medical record number, or M R N, or an authorized name.

18
00:00:55,968 --> 00:00:59,655
Open the patient record, then choose its saved treatment plan.

19
00:00:59,655 --> 00:01:05,640
Before going further, check the source, facility, record number, plan ID, and version.

20
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,607
A familiar name is a clue, not proof.

21
00:01:08,607 --> 00:01:11,259
Prefer to browse by plan status?

22
00:01:11,259 --> 00:01:14,491
Treatment Plans Roster is your other doorway.

23
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,828
Need to add documents?

24
00:01:16,828 --> 00:01:20,667
Open Manual Upload and look for Treatment-plan binder files.

25
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:26,172
Choose the approved files for one plan, then click Upload and securely process binder.

26
00:01:26,172 --> 00:01:30,439
Leave the separate JSON section to support unless they've asked you to use it.

27
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:35,351
Only enter an M R N correction when needed and checked against the source.

28
00:01:35,351 --> 00:01:40,919
Once processing finishes, read the warnings, then choose Review in Patient Roster.

29
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:43,577
Here's the easy to miss part.

30
00:01:43,577 --> 00:01:48,173
Stored safely and read successfully are two different things.

31
00:01:48,173 --> 00:01:52,731
Check how many files were parsed, and how many were stored without parsing.

32
00:01:52,731 --> 00:01:57,226
A photo can be tucked away safely without the app reading its contents.

33
00:01:57,226 --> 00:02:02,011
If you see that warning, check the original and ask support about a readable format.

34
00:02:02,011 --> 00:02:05,963
Uploaded does not automatically mean evaluated or compliant.

35
00:02:06,716 --> 00:02:09,052
Now open Treatment Plan Detail.

36
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:12,587
The status tells you where to look, not the whole story.

37
00:02:12,587 --> 00:02:15,580
Overdue, Urgent, or Due Soon?

38
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:16,842
Check the dates.

39
00:02:16,842 --> 00:02:19,544
Missing Data or Conflicting Evidence?

40
00:02:19,544 --> 00:02:21,135
Go back to the source.

41
00:02:21,135 --> 00:02:24,178
Needs Review or Unable to Evaluate?

42
00:02:24,178 --> 00:02:25,542
Get human help.

43
00:02:25,542 --> 00:02:29,216
Even Current or Compliant still needs a look at the checklist.

44
00:02:29,216 --> 00:02:33,875
Open the relevant row in the forty two step checklist to see why it was flagged.

45
00:02:33,875 --> 00:02:38,219
Level of care change rules are still awaiting R3 confirmation.

46
00:02:38,983 --> 00:02:45,725
Compare the dates, signatures, and source evidence, then use the review or comment controls your role allows.

47
00:02:45,725 --> 00:02:49,513
Keep your notes clear enough that the next person can follow your thinking.

48
00:02:49,513 --> 00:02:52,177
If an override is needed, explain why.

49
00:02:52,177 --> 00:02:55,801
It records your decision; it doesn't rewrite the source.

50
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:57,089
Missing a control?

51
00:02:57,089 --> 00:02:58,453
Ask your manager.

52
00:02:58,453 --> 00:03:02,619
Automatic source imports also need authorized, approved setup.

53
00:03:02,619 --> 00:03:04,804
You don't need to sort that out on your own.

54
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:11,328
And that's your first pass: find the plan, check the evidence, and record the next step.

55
00:03:11,328 --> 00:03:13,563
If you get stuck, Help is right there.

56
00:03:13,563 --> 00:03:14,876
An empty roster?

57
00:03:14,876 --> 00:03:17,502
Clear filters and check the source.

58
00:03:17,502 --> 00:03:18,878
Trouble signing in?

59
00:03:18,878 --> 00:03:23,777
Use Forgot password with your saved recovery code, or ask your administrator.

60
00:03:23,777 --> 00:03:29,131
If the page won't open, check the launcher and try localhost colon eight thousand.

61
00:03:29,131 --> 00:03:34,952
Give support the version and a safe error message, without patient details or passwords.

62
00:03:34,952 --> 00:03:37,490
Then sign out and lock Windows.

63
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:39,295
One plan at a time.

64
00:03:39,295 --> 00:03:40,823
You've got a place to start.
